<h2 id="ha-ctrl-007-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Compare a sensor-only appliance, a remotely enabled controller and a remotely disabled controller. Only supported commands may be available.
2. Exercise idle, running, paused, returning, docked, fault and unavailable states with valid zero, null and estimated duration values.
3. Delay or reject Pause/Return and preserve current native state; do not replay a command automatically after reconnection.
4. Verify task labels, keyboard access, quiet progress announcements and exact fault-code copying. Record the integration/device version and use a simulator for actions unless physical testing is explicitly planned.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

